WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.150
The Ganges at Patna, 1980.

2
00:00:03.200 --> 00:00:07.270
About 88 per cent of the year's
sediment moved in the monsoon.

3
00:00:07.320 --> 00:00:11.630
The monsoon carried 76 per
cent of the year's water.

4
00:00:11.680 --> 00:00:13.990
Faster water moves bigger grains.

5
00:00:14.040 --> 00:00:17.890
So you might expect the smallest
grains to be the easiest to lift.

6
00:00:17.940 --> 00:00:21.530
Yet silt, one-hundredth
the width of coarse sand,

7
00:00:21.580 --> 00:00:24.850
needs water about 3
times as fast to lift it.

8
00:00:24.900 --> 00:00:25.690
Why?

9
00:00:25.740 --> 00:00:27.030
Is silt heavier?

10
00:00:27.080 --> 00:00:29.270
Does it sink into gaps in the bed?

11
00:00:29.320 --> 00:00:31.410
In this mission, you'll measure discharge,

12
00:00:31.460 --> 00:00:34.650
and see how a river changes downstream.

13
00:00:34.700 --> 00:00:38.430
Then you'll read a famous graph
of grain size against water speed,

14
00:00:38.480 --> 00:00:41.830
showing erosion, transport and deposition.

15
00:00:41.880 --> 00:00:47.070
Your mission: explain why tiny silt grains
need faster water to lift than coarse

16
00:00:47.120 --> 00:00:47.880
sand.
